<title>UK: Finelist up after Sunday Times comment.</title>
<headline>Finelist up after Sunday Times comment.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finelist Group Plc Plc rose on Monday after a &quot;buy&quot; recommendation in the Sunday Times &quot;inside track&quot; column, dealers said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 7-1/2p at 370 by 0950 GMT.</p>
<p>The report said Finelist had moved quickly to establish itself as a big player in the fragmented auto products market.</p>
<p>Recent acquisitions should lift pre-tax profits to 24 million stg in 1998, up from 17 million last year, the report said, putting it on a prospecting price-earnings multiple of just fifteen times.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
